The following circuit is designed for general embedded applications, using the ATMEGA328P-AU as the microcontroller. U3 serves as the real-time clock, while U2 and U1 provide non-volatile storage.

The circuit is large enough to require a separate schematic layer to clearly illustrate the connection pins.

Datasheets of the ICs were carefully reviewed to select the correct crystal values and ensure stable oscillation. To improve mobility, the circuit is powered from a battery rather than a power adapter.

Challenges: The use of a four-layer PCB proved time-intensive and required careful consideration of trace placement to minimize noise and coupling, especially given the compact structure.
